"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010372396806008419,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.022669999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":15.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Interface, Inc. designs, produces, and sells modular carpet products in the United States, Canada, Latin America, Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia. The company offers modular carpets; luxury vinyl tiles; modular resilient flooring products; rubber flooring; and carpet tiles used in commercial interiors, include offices, educational facilities, healthcare facilities, airports, hospitality spaces, retail spaces, and residential interiors. It also provides carpet replacement, installation, and maintenance services; and other products and services, including TacTiles carpet tile installation system and adhesives and products for carpet installation and maintenance, as well as project management services. The company sells its products under the Interface, FLOR, NORAPLAN, and NORAMENT brands through direct sales to end users and indirect sales through independent contractors, installers and distributors. Interface, Inc. was incorporated in 1973 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Laurel M. Hurd | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $385K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $34K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Interface, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.9B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $122M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 38% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3842497460411503},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","19 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Investigates Claims On Behalf of Investors of Interface, Inc. - TILE","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-investigates-claims-on-behalf-of-investors-of-interface-inc---tile-302949000.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795705200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.447,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Interface (NASDAQ:TILE) Posted Healthy Earnings But There Are Some Other Factors To Be Aware Of","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nasdaq-tile/interface/news/interface-nasdaqtile-posted-healthy-earnings-but-there-are-s","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795002345.341,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.874,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Interface (TILE) Cheap After Trimming Its 2026 Sales Outlook?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nasdaq-tile/interface/news